      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "To explore the effect of endoscopic sinus surgery (ESS) in patients with chronic rhinosinusitis and asthma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Forty-two patients with asthma who underwent ESS and control group were investigated. Interleukin-4 (IL-4), interferon-gamma (IFN-gamma), soluble interleukin-2 receptor (sIL-2R) and soluble CD23 (sCD23) levels in culture supernatant of peripheral blood mononuclear cell (PBMC) were determined by enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Of these 42 patients 32 (76%), their asthma was relieved greatly after ESS comparing with that before ESS. 14 of 21 patients (67%) taken regular medication for asthma before ESS reported that less medicine was used after operation."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "This study demonstrates that ESS has a favorable effect on asthma in patients with symptomatic chronic sinusitis."
        }
      ]},
